    "body": "> My suspicion is that the error message is printed on stderr, while the version is printed on stdout, but because we smash them together in `internal_cmd_exec`, we can't separate them.\r\n\r\nI think it might be worse if I remember correctly `cmd_exec` keeps `stdout` and `stderr` separate so I think PHP is outputting this error to `stdout`. \r\n\r\n@selfagency can you run\r\n`$env:RUST_LOG=starship=trace; starship module php; Remove-Item Env:\\RUST_LOG` (hopefully I've got the powershell syntax right) and\r\n`php -r \"echo PHP_MAJOR_VERSION.'.'.PHP_MINOR_VERSION.'.'.PHP_RELEASE_VERSION;\"` in that directory and add the output here.",
