    "body": "```\r\n\r\n~\r\n❯ $env:RUST_LOG=starship=trace; starship module php; Remove-Item Env:\\RUST_LOG\r\nstarship=trace: The term 'starship=trace' is not recognized as the name of a cmdlet, function, script file, or operable program.\r\nCheck the spelling of the name, or if a path was included, verify that the path is correct and try again.\r\nRemove-Item: Cannot find path 'Env:\\RUST_LOG' because it does not exist.\r\n\r\n~ took 5s\r\n❯ php -r \"echo PHP_MAJOR_VERSION.'.'.PHP_MINOR_VERSION.'.'.PHP_RELEASE_VERSION;\"\r\n\r\nDeprecated: Directive 'track_errors' is deprecated in Unknown on line 0\r\n7.4.1\r\n\r\n~\r\n❯\r\n```\r\n\r\nAdding quotes around `starship=trace` fixed the above output.\r\n\r\n```\r\n❯ $env:RUST_LOG=\"starship=trace\"; starship module php; Remove-Item Env:\\RUST_LOG\r\n DEBUG starship::context > Unable to get path from $PWD: environment variable not found\r\n DEBUG starship::config  > STARSHIP_CONFIG is not set\r\n DEBUG starship::config  > Using default config path: C:\\Users\\dan\\.config/starship.toml\r\n DEBUG starship::config  > Unable to read config file content:\r\nThe system cannot find the file specified. (os error 2)\r\n TRACE starship::context > Building HashSets of directory files, folders and extensions took 5.0006ms\r\n\r\n~\r\n❯\r\n```",
