    "created_at": "2020-06-11T18:58:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-11T18:58:38Z",
    "body": "This really sounds like a misconfigured version of PHP, as the code that is running to print the version number does not trigger anything that would write out errors. Some potential ways I think Starship could get around this (if @selfagency could be so kind to test them to confirm):\r\n\r\n1. Run the command without local settings. These settings will not change anything about the raw PHP version anyway. This means running it with the `-n` flag:\r\n   \r\n   ```\r\n   php -nr \"echo PHP_MAJOR_VERSION.'.'.PHP_MINOR_VERSION.'.'.PHP_RELEASE_VERSION;\"\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n2. Run the command and explicitly hide all errors and warnings. This should overwrite whatever the local settings tell PHP to do. This means using the `-d` flag with an extra option:\r\n   \r\n   ```\r\n   php -d \"error_reporting=0\" -r \"echo PHP_MAJOR_VERSION.'.'.PHP_MINOR_VERSION.'.'.PHP_RELEASE_VERSION;\"\r\n   ```\r\n\r\nBoth of these options should easily fit within the `exec_cmd` part of the PHP module.\r\n\r\nBig fan of both Starship and PHP, hope this drive-by comment can help some people out 😄 ",
